meta {
  name: Get invoice PDF
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/invoices/:id/pdf
  auth: bearer
}

params:path {
  id: 1
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{partnerKey}}
}

docs {
  A **302** to a presigned link that expires in five minutes, not the bytes. The object store
  serves them, so a large download never occupies an application thread.

  Found rather than Moved Permanently on purpose: the link expires, and a cached permanent
  redirect would send you to a dead URL for ever. Follow it, do not store it.

  The PDF is rendered on first request and kept. A reprint is the same document — byte for byte
  — because "is this the invoice we sent?" has to have an answer.
}
